ull,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,null,300,1,0]}],"solution":"class HitCounter:\n    WINDOW = 300\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.q = deque()   # (timestamp, count) pairs, oldest first\n        self.total = 0\n\n    def hit(self, timestamp: int) -> None:\n        if self.q and self.q[-1][0] == timestamp:\n            self.q[-1][1] += 1\n        else:\n            self.q.append([timestamp, 1])\n        self.total += 1\n\n    def getHits(self, timestamp: int) -> int:\n        while self.q and self.q[0][0] <= timestamp - self.WINDOW:\n            self.total -= self.q.popleft()[1]\n        return self.total\n","approach":"**Key insight: the stream is chronological, so a queue of hits is automatically sorted and expiring old hits is just popping from the front.** Keep a deque of `(timestamp, count)` pairs and a running total. `hit` either bumps the count of the last pair (same second) or appends a new pair. `getHits` pops pairs whose timestamp is `<= timestamp - 300` and returns the total.\n\nEach hit is pushed once and popped at most once, so the work is amortised O(1) per call. Grouping hits by second bounds the deque at 300 entries no matter how many hits arrive.\n\nThe classic O(1)-memory alternative is a circular buffer of 300 slots: `times[t % 300]` and `counts[t % 300]`. On `hit`, if the stored time differs from `t`, reset the slot. On `getHits`, sum the counts of the slots whose stored time is inside the window, which is 300 additions regardless of volume.\n\n**Common mistakes:** off-by-one on the window (`timestamp - 300` must be excluded, `timestamp - 299` included); forgetting to evict inside `getHits` when no `hit` happened recently; popping on `hit` only, which leaves stale data if `getHits` is called far in the future.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** What if hits arrive out of order? (keep a sorted structure or bucket by second and sum.) What if there are millions of hits per second? (the bucket-per-second array is the answer; counts, not individual events.) Concurrency: a lock per call, or atomic counters per bucket; for a distributed counter, shard by server and sum on read, accepting slight staleness.","complexity":{"time":"O(1) amortised per call (O(300) worst case for the bucket variant)","space":"O(300) = O(1)"},"similar":["moving-average-from-data-stream","lru-cache"],"number":175}